{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T13:30:02.189Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e5330e1791f32ab2f4c04d76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T13:30:02.188Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) on PR #1680 head b0a334fa1: 2 findings on this item, both verified and fixed.\n(P2) Nested scopes: an outer clientA.withExpectedItemRevisions re-rendered (and added evidence to) a refusal raised by an inner clientB scope on another tracker. The guard now records the canonical tracker of each refusal it raises (itemRevisionRefusalTracker in src/core/store/item-mutation-precondition.ts), and re-created errors keep it (retainItemRevisionRefusalTracker). enrichItemRevisionConflict returns a refusal from another tracker unchanged, so the owning scope supplies both its evidence and its scoped commands.\n(P2) runAction with an explicit cwd rendered the caller's relative path, which names another tracker from the caller's process cwd. It now renders the resolved tracker root, including when cwd alone selected the tracker.\nSpecs: a two-tracker nested-scope case and a runAction explicit-cwd case in tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.spec.ts."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T13:30:02.189Z"}],"before_hash":"32edfd218b6939a6b20a8ce521dddfac856a5af9814c02d27672b1a810d16bfe","after_hash":"8b3e68e54fb2673fe997737193070d48a38dfc7b283e75f86fc966bfb925389b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9a888a22a457d42bfc5eecbd08d210b39dcdda631af5aada56c18915da3bb6cd"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T14:30:55.084Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e5330e1791f32ab2f4c04d76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T14:30:55.083Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 on PR #1680 head dc8cad9be (Codex gpt-6.1-sol xhigh, 4 findings; CodeRabbit full review, 6 findings). Fixed:\n(1) Refusal ownership is shared across SDK bundle graphs through the global registry (Symbol.for @unbrained/pm-cli/item-revision-refusal-trackers), like the scope registry.\n(2) Ownership is recovered from the cause chain, so a composition wrapper (finishComposition) still belongs to the inner tracker.\n(3) PmClient recovery keeps --no-extensions for a client created with noExtensions true. An active-extension-host client, which disables extensions only internally, does not get it.\n(4) The output encoding is explicit. ItemRevisionRecoveryInvocation.outputArgs replaces the json flag, the CLI renders --output-format <fmt> ahead of --json (the canonical flag wins, as for the invocation's own output), and runAction carries a requested outputFormat.\n(5) Close's post-close fan-out report now renders its examples with commandScope instead of inheriting the store refusal's unscoped reads.\n(6) docs/COMMANDS.md now says the recovery reads are live, not pinned to current_revision.\nNot changed: CodeRabbit's note that the pm package manage freshness check should distrust the registry record. That concerns package management, not this change; the record was written by pm package install of 2026.11.5 in this branch.\nFull suite 12118 passed, coverage 100/100/100/100."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T14:30:55.084Z"}],"before_hash":"8b3e68e54fb2673fe997737193070d48a38dfc7b283e75f86fc966bfb925389b","after_hash":"4769b00f43597b82d0559b3a24e6260ec3e2a0748f2b5c1fecc074a58f92b8d1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b13e9b4780545eca77281f149a633dde565d6488280da448cdc7650297cc8a5a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T15:15:51.160Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e5330e1791f32ab2f4c04d76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T15:15:51.160Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 on PR #1680 head 6107aeac8 (Codex): runAction derived --no-extensions from the global options of an active-extension-host client, which disables extensions only internally. Replaying the recovery would then hide extension item types. revisionRecoveryScopeArgs in src/sdk/runtime.ts now excludes that internal flag, the same exclusion PmClient.withExpectedItemRevisions uses. The spec drives PmClient.forActiveExtensionHost().run with expectHash, and forcing the flag back fails it (negative control)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T15:15:51.160Z"}],"before_hash":"4769b00f43597b82d0559b3a24e6260ec3e2a0748f2b5c1fecc074a58f92b8d1","after_hash":"35ed23de49a1bfce03539c9d85beaab8d39cfae928a7fda900deada0e2732b8f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b27aba4edd8a80accd5f9ad0c7c183d6d1fb7ff60e08dc86f9bab9f8d9c49bdc"}
